+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm install` then `pnpm start`. After editing diagnostics, run `pnpm build`
+and commit the generated `assets/inp-diagnostics.js` with the source. The bundle
+is included so the static page needs no CDN or runtime bundler.
+Run `pnpm test` for diagnostic serialization and transport checks.
+
+## INP diagnostics
+
+The page uses `web-vitals/attribution` to measure INP. It emits an
+`inp-diagnostic` event on `window` when the INP candidate changes and when the
+library finalizes a changed measurement as the page becomes hidden.
+Needs-improvement and poor results also produce console warnings.
+No interaction means there may be no INP report.
+
+For field collection, set `data-report-url` on the script in `index.html` to an
+existing analytics ingestion endpoint. This repository has no analytics server;
+the empty default keeps reports local. The endpoint must accept POST bodies
+containing JSON with a `text/plain` content type. Delivery uses `sendBeacon`,
+falling back to `fetch` with `keepalive`; delivery is best effort. Cross-origin
+endpoints must permit this origin for the fetch fallback.
+
+Reports contain the metric ID, value and rating, all three delay phases, the
+interaction target and type, document load state, and available script/layout/
+paint attribution. Store the latest report per metric ID rather than summing
+values: updates revise the page's INP, not separate interactions.
+
+Use `largestDelayPhase` to start investigating:
+
+- `inputDelay`: inspect work occupying the main thread before handlers run.
+- `processingDuration`: inspect interaction event handlers.
+- `presentationDelay`: inspect rendering, layout, and work before the next paint.
+
+`longestScript` identifies an overlapping script with its source location,
+function, forced-layout time, and overlapping delay phase when available.
+These are clues, not proof that the script caused the full delay.
+Browsers without Long Animation Frames still report INP and its phases, with
+`longestScript: null`. Browsers without Event Timing skip instrumentation.
+
+Targets use static `data-inp-target` labels, falling back to element tag names.
+Do not put visitor data in these labels. Reports exclude input values, DOM text,
+page URLs, and script URL queries/fragments. Script paths and function names
+remain available to locate problematic code.
